{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1396887-technocracy-infiltration-in-public-institutions","id":1396887,"title":"Technocracy infiltration in public institutions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-06-16T09:10:52-07:00","id":1396887,"title":"Technocracy infiltration in public institutions","content":"Hello everyone,<br /> <br /> That the technocracy has a lot of influence in the government is something we all know. The thing is I'm curious about how to reflect this: Just how far does this influence reach? What is the level of infiltration? What form does this influence take (direct orders, bribery, blackmail, all of them, etc...) Are the higher ups of the government aware of it? Does the technocracy have agents directly working inside public institutions? If so, does the technocracy have enlightened agents infiltrated or do they leave that to just regular and extraordinary agents? I'm not looking for a definitive answer, I just want to know your opinions.<br /> <br /> Thanks in advance.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-16T09:56:53-07:00","id":1396893,"title":"","content":"In my games, the Technocracy tends to find organizations most suited to their plans and quietly infiltrate them. This has been going on for a while such that truly important organizations will have technocrats as part of the groups topmost leadership and sometimes pretty much having all the most important positions filled by technocrats, especially if the organization leadership is a relatively small group. <br /> <br /> This puts a fair number of NWO agents in key positions in government, media, and law enforcement. Enough to give the impression of having eyes everywhere even though they really don't. The syndicate will likewise have members who are part of the bigger financial institutions, own the bigger big businesses, and have a say in those rich boys clubs type things, or whatever you call them. ITX will be in the more influential or potentially influential tech or industrial groups, military weapons development, robotics and computer stuff. Progenitors will have a control of major medical institutions,hospitals, pharmacies, related govt offices, etc. And void engineers will be in control of aerospace groups, space science centers, aquatic research, and geological survey groups, etc. Not to mention Technocracy recruiters hiding in schools working as faculty or in relevant job recruitment centers. <br /> <br /> Now since they can't be everywhere at once and only a fraction of the Technocracy would be suited for this sort of cold war spy like stuff, this stretches the number of them in these places fairly thin, though it also occasionally concentrates them in some areas. <br /> <br /> For example it would be possible to attend a conference that the NWO is using as an excuse to get their law enforcement and media infiltrators in the same place as their Syndicate financial backers regarding something developed by one of the other conventions. <br /> <br /> Most of the time though, each organization deemed important enough to infiltrate will be doing work for the tech without knowing it and maybe have a smaller number of those in the know but not enlightened who outright answer to their enlightened Technocracy bosses.<br /> <br /> Bribery and blackmail comes in when the organization or it's agents must be made to act in an anomalous manner for the good of the Technocracy and things can't be handled directly by enlightened staff or else bribery and blackmail or other influence or coercion is just easier. Like say when a sheriff can be made to shut up about a werewolf attack with a threat and a bribe . Maybe a technocrat with high levels of mind will fix things up better later but they might not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-18T06:56:17-07:00","id":1397279,"title":"","content":"It's worth remembering that a person can be a Technocracy asset and be more or less ignorant of whom they serve, if they realize they serve anyone (else) at all.<br /> <br /> They may assume their &quot;boss&quot; (that is, the one giving them Technocracy orders) is simply a person so far up the chain of command of their usual organization as to be top secret.<br /> <br /> They might &quot;know&quot; they are serving something akin to the Illuminati, but be totally ignorant of what, exactly, they are.<br /> <br /> They may be a Manchurian agent, with programming planted in their minds, to be activated at the Union's choosing or in response to prearranged scenarios.<br /> <br /> Even agents &quot;in the fold&quot; don't get the full picture, if they aren't Enlightened. (In fact, not even then). Not every agent placed on a corporation's board of directors is a full Mage, or even an Extraordinary Citizen.<br /> <br /> There are levels of clearance for knowledge, as there is with any competent conspiracy. The Union keeps its assets on a Need-To-Know basis. The Technocracy couldn't be half as successful (or secretive) as it is without this kind of clandestine activity. If they can get away with merely co-opting (or programming) an otherwise unrelated asset, it's more efficient than relying on &quot;full members&quot;.<br /> <br /> Of course, with this gain in coverage comes an incremental loss of control. If the agent, contact, or pawn doesn't know anything, they can't reveal anything. But they also can't necessarily do all you'd like without more heavy supervision and the potential for exposure. Especially problematic when an asset would rebel if they understood what they really served.<br /> <br /> To a certain extent, much of the power the Union has lies in their ability to gather information. A pawn need know nothing if they just have to report in. Not even that they're a pawn, or that they do any reporting. (There's that bit about Manchurian agents again). If the Union knows something out of the ordinary is going on, they can take steps to investigate further and correct where needed.<br /> <br /> Another facet of Technocratic control is their ability to make people serve the interests of the Union, unknowingly but of their own will. Law and order, free exercise of business, exploration, secrecy, etc. The Union makes people believe in their cause, so they go about doing the Union's will independently. This has the added benefit - if not the Union's main goal as a Mage organization - of perpetuating and reinforcing their Paradigm. More even than wanting to make everyone puppets, the Union desires for Sleepers to be Technocrats <i>in their hearts and minds</i>.<br /> <br /> If they can do that, the Union will win.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":6156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","user":"Bluecho","date":". 06-18-2020, 09:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}